{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2170-03-19 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning, Mrs. ___ . I’m Dr. ___ , part of the orthopaedic team. You’re here today for your left total shoulder replacement, correct?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2170-03-19 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, that’s right. I’ve been in pain for so long — it’s hard to lift anything, even a coffee cup."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2170-03-19 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I understand. The X-rays showed bone-on-bone arthritis in your shoulder joint, which explains the pain. The surgery should help significantly."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2170-03-19 09:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I had the same thing done on my right shoulder a few years ago, and it worked well. I’m hopeful this one will too."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2170-03-19 09:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s a good sign. You’ve recovered well before, so we expect a similar outcome. We’ll go over the risks — infection, nerve injury, blood clots — but overall it’s a safe procedure."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2170-03-19 09:10:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m allergic to aspirin and shellfish — just wanted to make sure that’s noted."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2170-03-19 09:11:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, it’s in your chart. We’ll avoid any medications with those components. Any other concerns before we head to surgery?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2170-03-19 09:13:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No, I think I’m ready. Just want to get through this."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2170-03-19 09:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re all set. The team will take you to the operating room shortly. We’ll see you afterward."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2170-03-19 14:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Mrs. ___ , you’re back on the floor. The surgery went very well — your new shoulder joint is in place, and you were stable the whole time."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2170-03-19 14:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s a relief. Is there a lot of pain? I feel a bit groggy."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2170-03-19 14:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re on pain medication through the IV. We’ll switch to pills soon. The incision looks good — no swelling or drainage."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2170-03-19 14:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good. I was worried about infection — I’ve had health issues before."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2170-03-19 14:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re monitoring closely. Your vitals are stable, and your blood work shows no signs of infection yet."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2170-03-20 08:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. How’s the pain today? On a scale of 1 to 10?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2170-03-20 08:32:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "About a 6. It’s better than yesterday, but still uncomfortable."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2170-03-20 08:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s expected. We’ll keep adjusting your meds. Your hemoglobin is a bit low — 9.2 — so we’re watching for anemia, but no transfusion needed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2170-03-20 08:36:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve been tired lately. Is that from the blood count?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2170-03-20 08:38:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Partly, yes. Surgery and blood loss can cause that. We’ll help it improve with nutrition and rest."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2170-03-20 08:40:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. What about my other medicines — like for blood pressure and asthma?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2170-03-20 08:42:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re back on lisinopril and metoprolol. For asthma, you can use your inhaler as needed. We switched from Advair to fluticasone-salmeterol — same thing, different brand."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2170-03-20 08:44:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. And my cholesterol pill?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2170-03-20 08:45:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Pravastatin — we lowered the dose to 20 mg daily. We’ll keep an eye on your liver function."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2170-03-21 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. You had a slight fever last night — nothing high, but we checked a urine sample."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2170-03-21 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Oh, I felt a little warm. Is something wrong?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2170-03-21 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The urine showed white blood cells, which suggests a mild urinary tract infection. But the culture came back negative — no bacteria grew."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2170-03-21 09:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So do I need antibiotics?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2170-03-21 09:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re prescribing a short course — trimethoprim-sulfamethoxazole for 7 days — just to be safe, since you had symptoms."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2170-03-21 09:10:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. I’ve had UTIs before — they can get bad if not treated."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2170-03-21 09:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. We’re being cautious. Your temperature is normal now, which is a good sign."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2170-03-21 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The physical therapist saw you this morning. How did it go?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2170-03-21 10:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "We did some gentle pendulum exercises. It felt strange, but not painful."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2170-03-21 10:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s perfect. You’ll keep doing those at home. No weight on the left arm — use the sling at all times."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2170-03-21 10:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I remember from my last surgery. It’s frustrating, but I know it’s important."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2170-03-22 08:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Morning. Your labs are stable. Hemoglobin improved slightly to 9.8. White count is still a bit high, but likely from surgery, not infection."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2170-03-22 08:32:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So I’m healing okay?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2170-03-22 08:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes. Incision is clean, neurovascular checks are good — sensation and movement are intact. Grip is weaker on the left, but expected after surgery."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2170-03-22 08:36:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And the UTI? Is the antibiotic helping?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2170-03-22 08:38:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "No fever today, and you’re not having urgency or burning — so yes, it’s working. Finish the full course."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2170-03-22 08:40:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will do. When can I go home?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2170-03-22 08:42:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "If all goes well, tomorrow morning. You’ll have home physical therapy and follow-up in two weeks."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2170-03-22 08:44:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ll need help at home, but my nephew can stay for a few days."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2170-03-22 08:46:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s great. Make sure you don’t lift anything or use the left arm to push up from bed or chair."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2170-03-22 08:48:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I remember — ‘no weight bearing.’ I’ll be careful."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2170-03-23 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good news — you’re cleared to go home today. Your incision is healing well, and you’re stable."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2170-03-23 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s wonderful. What about my pain medicine?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2170-03-23 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ll take oxycodone-acetaminophen as needed for pain — up to every 4 hours, but no more than 10 in 24 hours. Don’t mix with alcohol."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2170-03-23 09:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my other meds — should I restart them all?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2170-03-23 09:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, all your usual medications — blood pressure, asthma, cholesterol, and the UTI antibiotic for the next 6 days."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2170-03-23 09:10:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And when do I see Dr. ___ again?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 51,
      "time": "2170-03-23 09:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "In two weeks. They’ll check the incision and possibly remove the staples. Call sooner if you have redness, fever over 101, or increased pain."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 52,
      "time": "2170-03-23 09:14:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. Thank you — I’m feeling hopeful."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 53,
      "time": "2170-03-23 09:16:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ve done well. Keep doing the pendulum exercises, wear the sling, and let your body heal. You’re on the right path."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 54,
      "time": "2170-03-23 09:18:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ll take it one day at a time."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 55,
      "time": "2170-03-23 09:20:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s the best way. We’ll see you in clinic soon."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 56,
      "time": "2170-03-23 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "One more thing — my asthma has been a little worse. Should I be worried?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 57,
      "time": "2170-03-23 10:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re on your inhalers — albuterol as needed, and the fluticasone-salmeterol twice daily. If you’re using albuterol more than twice a week, call your pulmonologist."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 58,
      "time": "2170-03-23 10:04:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, I’ll watch that."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 59,
      "time": "2170-03-23 10:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Also, continue the fexofenadine for allergies — it’s now twice daily instead of loratadine once daily. Might help with breathing too."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 60,
      "time": "2170-03-23 10:08:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. So many pills, but I’ll manage."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 61,
      "time": "2170-03-23 10:10:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll send a full list home with you. And remember — no smoking. It slows healing and worsens asthma."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 62,
      "time": "2170-03-23 10:12:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I know… I’ve been trying to quit. This stay made me think about it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 63,
      "time": "2170-03-23 10:14:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s a great step. Talk to your doctor about support — patches, counseling. Your lungs and heart will thank you."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 64,
      "time": "2170-03-23 10:16:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. One health thing at a time."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 65,
      "time": "2170-03-23 10:18:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. You’re doing great. Discharge papers are ready — nurse will go over them with you."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 66,
      "time": "2170-03-23 10:20:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you, Doctor. I appreciate everything."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 67,
      "time": "2170-03-23 10:22:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. Take care, and we’ll see you soon."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2170-03-19 08:30:00",
    "admission_end": "2170-03-23 13:04:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "Mrs. ___ was admitted for elective left total shoulder arthroplasty due to severe osteoarthritis causing debilitating pain. The surgery was performed successfully, and she remained hemodynamically stable throughout. Post-operatively, she experienced mild anemia and a transient fever on post-operative day 2, prompting a urine test that showed leukocytes but no bacterial growth on culture. She was treated with a short course of trimethoprim-sulfamethoxazole for a presumed urinary tract infection. Pain was well controlled, and she progressed with physical therapy, performing pendulum exercises and maintaining non-weight-bearing status. She was discharged home with home physical therapy, instructions for wound care, and follow-up in two weeks. Her chronic conditions, including asthma, hypertension, hyperlipidemia, rheumatoid arthritis, and history of breast cancer, were managed during admission, and medication adjustments were made, including a reduction in pravastatin dose and a change in allergy medication. Tobacco use was addressed, and she expressed interest in quitting.",
    "problems": [
      "Osteoarthrosis, localized, not specified whether primary or secondary, shoulder region",
      "Urinary tract infection, site not specified",
      "Asthma, unspecified type, unspecified",
      "Personal history of malignant neoplasm of breast",
      "Unspecified essential hypertension",
      "Other and unspecified hyperlipidemia",
      "Rheumatoid arthritis",
      "Tobacco use disorder"
    ]
  }
}
